// Golden vectors for the fee-payer signing message, produced by the Aptos TS SDK
// via Aptos-Contracts/tools/wallet-check (generateSigningMessageForTransaction).
//
// A DIFFERENT implementation is the point: if the Go encoder reproduces these
// bytes, the hand-written struct layout matches the reference one for this shape.
//
// The shape is the PRODUCTION one, unlike milestone 1:
//   - SIX proof elements, so the vector<vector<u8>> path is exercised non-empty
//   - sequence_number 258, which is multi-byte and would catch a u64 endianness
//     error that 0 cannot
//   - both fee-payer forms: the sender signing 0x0, and the sender signing the
//     real payer address
//
// Regenerate with tools/wallet-check/genvec.mjs if the encoding ever legitimately
// changes. Do NOT edit these bytes to make a test pass: they are the oracle.
